   "plaque": "arts_shakespeare",
   "theme": "arts",
   "title": "William Shakespeare",
   "text": "William Shakespeare was baptised in Stratford-upon-Avon in April 1564, came to London as an actor and playwright, and died on 23 April 1616. His company built the first Globe in 1599; it burned down in 1613 when a stage cannon set the thatch alight during Henry VIII. In 1623 two of his fellow actors gathered thirty-six plays into the First Folio, without which half of them would be lost. 'All the world's a stage,' he wrote, 'and all the men and women merely players.' The groundlings would like a word about the men and women merely standing."
  }
